Subject: [PATCH] libvirt: do not request ACPI on ppc64 and s390 guests

nova's _set_features() adds the ACPI feature unconditionally for the qemu
and kvm virt types, with no architecture check. The ppc64 "pseries" and
s390 "s390-ccw-virtio" machine types have no ACPI at all - they use a
device tree / SCLP instead - and libvirt >= 10 validates this and refuses
the domain:

    libvirt.libvirtError: unsupported configuration: machine type
    'pseries-10.0' does not support ACPI

Older libvirt silently ignored the flag, which is why this only surfaces
now (this build ships libvirt 11.3 and QEMU 10.0). The effect is total:
no instance can be spawned on a ppc64le compute node, every build fails
in _create_guest_with_network and is rescheduled until it errors.

APIC has an escape hatch for exactly this class of problem
([workarounds] libvirt_disable_apic) but ACPI has none, so there is no
configuration-only fix and the source has to be corrected.

The guest architecture is read with libvirt_utils.get_arch(image_meta),
which is the idiom already used elsewhere in this file, so images that
set hw_architecture are honoured rather than assuming the host arch.

Applied against the installed copy in the venv, because the nova-base
Dockerfile runs kolla_patch after `pip install /nova`. Path uses the
version-independent `python3` symlink created in
docker/openstack-base/Dockerfile.j2.

--- var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/nova/virt/libvirt/driver.py
+++ var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/nova/virt/libvirt/driver.py
@@ -6729,7 +6729,16 @@
                 image_meta.properties.get('img_hide_hypervisor_id'))
 
         if CONF.libvirt.virt_type in ('qemu', 'kvm'):
-            guest.add_feature(vconfig.LibvirtConfigGuestFeatureACPI())
+            # ppc64 (pseries) and s390 (s390-ccw-virtio) machine types have
+            # no ACPI, and libvirt >= 10 rejects the domain instead of
+            # ignoring the flag, so it must not be requested there.
+            if libvirt_utils.get_arch(image_meta) not in (
+                    fields.Architecture.PPC64LE,
+                    fields.Architecture.PPC64,
+                    fields.Architecture.PPC,
+                    fields.Architecture.S390X,
+                    fields.Architecture.S390):
+                guest.add_feature(vconfig.LibvirtConfigGuestFeatureACPI())
             if not CONF.workarounds.libvirt_disable_apic:
                 guest.add_feature(vconfig.LibvirtConfigGuestFeatureAPIC())
 
